==Finnish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*hek}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-fpr-pro|*sej}}. Cognates include {{cog|se|sii}}, {{cog|myv|сынь}}. The word is inflected as plural, but there is no plural marker in the nominative, except in dialects ({{m|fi|het}}).

====Pronunciation====
{{fi-pronunciation|a=fi-he.ogg}}

====Pronoun====
{{fi-pron}}

# {{lb|fi|personal}} [[they]] {{qualifier|plural, only of people}}
# {{lb|fi|respectful}} [[he]], [[she]], [[one]], (singular) [[they]] {{q|of a single [[human being]]}} (Compare the usage of {{m|fi|hän}}.)

=====Usage notes=====
* In standard Finnish, '''''he''''' is practically never omitted, despite the verb showing both the person and the number. (Compare the usage of {{m|fi|hän}}, "she" / "he" / "they" (singular) / "one".)

=====Declension=====
* Irregular. The [[comitative]] and [[instructive]] forms don't exist; the [[abessive]] is hardly used.
* In addition to the standard set of cases, '''''he''''' and other personal pronouns have a specific [[accusative]] form; ''[[heidät]]''.
{{fi-decl-pron|1s=[[hän]]|2s=[[hänen]]|3s=[[häntä]]|4s=[[hänet]]|5s=[[hänessä]]|6s=[[hänestä]]|7s=[[häneen]]|8s=[[hänellä]]|9s=[[häneltä]]|10s=[[hänelle]]|11s=[[hänenä]]|12s=[[häneksi]]|14s=[[hänettä]]|1p='''he'''|2p=[[heidän]]|3p=[[heitä]]|4p=[[heidät]]|5p=[[heissä]]|6p=[[heistä]]|7p=[[heihin]]|8p=[[heillä]]|9p=[[heiltä]]|10p=[[heille]]|11p=[[heinä]]|12p=[[heiksi]]|14p=[[heittä]]|adv=no}}

